\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Held-out PPL as a function of fixed sharpening exponent $b$ (grid search, $\rho {=}0.4$). Seed\,42 provides the full nine-point sweep (circles); cross-seed markers at $b{=}0.5$ (triangles) confirm the plateau region. The shaded region marks $b \geq 2$ where PPL degrades past the uniform baseline; ESS-only $b^*$ (overall mean ${\approx }$3.5) falls in this degradation zone, while adaptive $b^*$ (mean ${\approx }$0.9) operates near the curve minimum.}}{5}{figure.caption.17}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:grid_b_trend}{{4}{5}{Held-out PPL as a function of fixed sharpening exponent $b$ (grid search, $\rho {=}0.4$). Seed\,42 provides the full nine-point sweep (circles); cross-seed markers at $b{=}0.5$ (triangles) confirm the plateau region. The shaded region marks $b \geq 2$ where PPL degrades past the uniform baseline; ESS-only $\bstar $ (overall mean ${\approx }$3.5) falls in this degradation zone, while adaptive $\bstar $ (mean ${\approx }$0.9) operates near the curve minimum}{figure.caption.17}{}}
